{
    "@visokiotype": "CustomBlockSchema.CustomBlockManifest",
    "name": "RFM Segmentation",
    "scriptFilename": "script.py",
    "language": "PYTHON",
    "executableVersion": null,
    "minVersions": [
        null
    ],
    "optionsVersion": 1,
    "apiVersion": "VERSION_0",
    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Scores customers on recency, frequency and monetary value from transactions and assigns named segments such as Champions, At Risk and Lost, with a segment summary.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Marketing",
    "tags": [
        "rfm",
        "segmentation",
        "customers",
        "crm",
        "marketing",
        "retention",
        "churn",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Turns a transactions table into a **customer segmentation** marketers can act on, using the classic RFM method:\n\n- **Recency**: days since the customer last bought (relative to an analysis date, by default the day after the latest transaction)\n- **Frequency**: number of orders (distinct order IDs, or rows if no order field is chosen)\n- **Monetary**: total spend\n\nEach is scored 1 to 5 (or 1 to N) by percentile, where 5 is best (most recent, most frequent, highest spend), giving an RFM score such as *543*. Customers are then placed in one of ten named segments:\n\n*Champions, Loyal Customers, Potential Loyalists, New Customers, Need Attention, About to Sleep, At Risk, Can't Lose Them, Hibernating, Lost*\n\nbased on their recency score and the average of their frequency and monetary scores. The second output summarises each segment (customers, revenue, shares, averages) with a description and a suggested action.\n\nThe segment rules are a widely used starting point, not a standard: the scores are in the output, so you can define your own segments with a formula.",
    "dependencies": "",
